<!--Post: 583--><!--Time: 1090827111-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST583"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:toadieskids@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->toadie<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, July 26, 2004 - 12:31 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK, <BR>I have been praying for you to do the right thing, and get this over with asap... <BR>We want to hear your story, and you want us to know, and I am sure  you are very anxious to tell us, so therefore what are you waiting for? <BR> <BR>It would not be very wise to try and kill someone now, because you would most likely be killed then we may never know your story, and that would not make us or YOU happy.... <BR> <BR>Please turn yourself in, and let us all &#40;including yourself&#41;, be safe and happy!!!!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 583-->
<!--Post: 840--><!--Time: 1093060012-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST840"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, August 20, 2004 - 8:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK: Are you color blind? 6% of males of European decent are color blind. a genetic anomaly, you know. <BR> <BR>ACL, what do you think?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 840-->
<!--Post: 849--><!--Time: 1093109933-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST849"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->ACL<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, August 21, 2004 - 10:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dear BTK, <BR> <BR>Short answers to the queries: <BR> <BR>1&#41; Problems with red/green color perception, but NOT completely color blind, as in only being able to see the grey scale. <BR> <BR>2&#41; Mixed parentage.  Enrollment records were the linchpin of my initial investigation.  From there, I went to your business records and am now monitoring your plastic and paper trails.  Dang, you sure like expensive toys. <BR> <BR>3&#41; Z used a .22 pistol with LR ammo in the Stine killing.  I trust what he told his &#34;roomie&#34;, who was my client, far more than any disinformation the police have issued.  According to my client, Z carried a black satchel, like a Dr.&#39;s bag, which contained a change of clothes, the .22 pistol, Stines car keys and shirttail wrapped in waxed paper.  According to my client, Foukes and Zelms did make contact with Z and he told them he was returning home for the night. Someone should check with the three witnesses and ask if Z was carrying a black bag.  If they say that he was, perhaps Foukes is basking in the limelight of his own incompetence.  The alleged reason that he wiped down the cab was that, at that time, he was still using scotch tape around his fingertips to mask his prints and one of the tapes fell off.  At one time, he used airplane glue, except that it gave him contact dermatitis. Then, several months later, he discovered that women&#39;s clear nail polish over his fingertips worked quite well.  <BR> <BR>4&#41; Tommie should be safe, so long as he comes prepared and uses protection.   However, I&#39;ll bet that you&#39;ll shove another banana up his tail pipe at every opportunity.  What&#39;s next, love poems? <BR> <BR>LE is tracing my IP&#39;s and there aren&#39;t enough Starbucks to go around.  Cannot stay on the net and risk getting popped for a felony.  Will answer future questions through the mail drop. <BR> <BR>Keep those btk babies sleepy and if you need any splash to keep them happy, just drop a line. I can respond in &#34;yes&#34;, &#34;no&#34; fashion to each numbered question at Kansas.com, under thread titles and monikers of your choosing. <BR> <BR>ACL <BR>   <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 849-->
<!--Post: 850--><!--Time: 1093126396-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST850"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Doone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Doone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, August 21, 2004 - 3:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey ACL. You have the most vivid yet extremely optimistic fantasy life of anyone I&#39;ve encountered while BTK sleuthing. Good luck with your meanderings. <BR>To BTK: <BR>Make sure and be quite clear when hurrying to respond to ACL,I think that he&#39;s running out of parlor tricks to accept your much anticipated response. Please, in the memory of Dr Wyatt, appease him. He has accused so many of being you, I&#39;m afraid he&#39;s going to blow a brain gasket. Thanks in advance.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 850-->
<!--Post: 856--><!--Time: 1093213968-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST856"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->A gerber baby<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, August 22, 2004 - 3:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have several questions about the attorney and his posting. <BR>1&#41;  How can you adequately listen and represent him? <BR>2&#41;  Is there a difference between attorney/client privilege and turning him on murder warrants? <BR>3&#41;  Is it a death penalty case? <BR>4&#41;  Can yourself and a counselor be protected by client privelege and the law if you don&#39;t turn him in when there are possible felony charges taht carry very serious felony charges with possibly very steep penalties? <BR> <BR>I would think that there is a difference between attorney/counselor/client privelege and not turning this man in as a murderer.  I am not an attorney or a couselor.  I do not know what the law is.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 856-->
<!--Post: 857--><!--Time: 1093214179-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST857"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->A gerber baby<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, August 22, 2004 - 3:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->By the way I am not trying to be antagonistic to anyone. <BR> <BR>Nor Am I BTK or a fan.  I am just very curious as to what makes a serial Killer and what it takes to counsel people or represent them as an attorney.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 857-->
<!--Post: 859--><!--Time: 1093218812-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST859"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, August 22, 2004 - 4:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nobody will test/compare evidence for DNA without good reason. So far, no good reason has been given.  <BR> <BR>Send me something concrete and we can go from there.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 859-->
<!--Post: 862--><!--Time: 1093238229-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST862"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, August 22, 2004 - 10:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->So, the Zodiac Killer had a roommate who told ACL the entire story?  Sounds like BS to me, and even if it did happen, it&#39;s no wonder that he&#39;s completely ignorant of the facts of the case.  Not only that, he had a hunch, checked enrollment records and discovered the true identity of BTK???  Wow, this sounds <i>exactly</i> like Gareth Penn having a hunch, researching biographies of sculptors at the Napa library, and discovering the true identity of the Zodiac Killer. &#60;yawn&#62; What a load of bullpucky. <BR> <BR>ACL wrote: <BR> <BR><font color="ff0000">LE is tracing my IP&#39;s and there aren&#39;t enough Starbucks to go around. Cannot stay on the net and risk getting popped for a felony.</font> <BR> <BR>He&#39;s truly living in a fantasy world.  I sincerely doubt law enforcement cares about this crackpot, and if he is what he says he is, then he knows he&#39;s breaking the law.  I guess now we know why they&#39;re called <b>criminal</b> lawyers...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 862-->
<!--Post: 864--><!--Time: 1093238616-->
